                <noteGrp type="abstract">
                    <desc xml:lang="en">Abstract</desc>
                    <note corresp="http://syriaca.org/nhsl" type="abstract" xml:lang="en" resp="http://syriaca.org">The second part of <persName ref="http://syriaca.org/person/239">Bar Hebraeus</persName>' 
                        <title xml:lang="en" ref="http://syriaca.org/work/2500">Chronicle</title>; an account of ecclesiastical history, starting with the 
                        biblical priest <persName ref="http://syriaca.org/person/1534">Aaron</persName> and continuing through <persName ref="http://syriaca.org/person/239">Bar Hebraeus</persName>' 
                        own time (the 13th century).</note>
                </noteGrp>
                <noteGrp type="contents">
                    <desc xml:lang="en">Contents</desc>
                    <note type="content" source="#bib2502-3" xml:lang="en">Section 1 of the Ecclesiastical History looks primarily west, to the history of the Church
                        in the Eastern Roman Empire and of the West Syrian patriarchs, while section 2 deals with the east, the West Syrian maphrians and the Church of the East 
                        patriarchs. The greatest value of the chronicle as a historical source is in its perspective on events in the east during Bar Hebraeus' lifetime in 
                        the 13th century.</note>
                </noteGrp>
